  "body": "## What\n\n- Adds `legacySelect(sessionId, lookup, value)` to `SessionGateway` and implements `select` and `legacySelect` on the Selenium and Playwright gateways.\n- `select` reads every `<option>` with its handle in one script, runs the option matcher, and clicks the matched handle. Matcher and Selenium reader are imported from `selenium-shared/select`.\n- `legacySelect` types the value into a closed native `<select>`, or runs the legacy click cascade, the keystrokes, and Enter on any other control.\n\n## Why\n\n- `session.select@1` threw `UnsupportedSessionOperationError` on Selenium, and the Ferrara upload path needs one select.\n- The [BE-3483](https://linear.app/sola-ai/issue/BE-3483) decision record keeps both legacy select paths as two actions, implemented by [BE-3519](https://linear.app/sola-ai/issue/BE-3519).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Matcher and Selenium reader are imported from `selenium-shared/select`, so `session.select@1` inherits fixes to that still-improving validation work.\n- `legacy-click-cascade.ts` and `legacy-scrape-read.ts` stay copies: DSL-IR is leaving those behaviors behind.\n- DSL-owned: the 250 ms re-read, the typed errors, the Playwright reader.\n- `select` throws `NotNativeSelectError`, or `SelectOptionMatchError` with `noMatchingOption`, `ambiguousOption`, or `optionDisabled`.\n- Ambiguity fails at once. The other two re-read every 250 ms inside the allowance.\n- Neither method clicks a native `<select>` first, as legacy since #17122.\n- Playwright `legacySelect` clicks once, no cascade, and types through `page.keyboard`.\n- Playwright `select` uses `selectOption({ index, value })`, so a drifted list throws.\n- Additive except Playwright `select`, which now runs the shared matcher instead of `selectOption(value)`.\n\n## Examples\n\nGateway calls against the `select.html` fixture, whose `#ferrara` control carries the seven options of Ferrara's `select#test-report-action0`.\n\n```ts\nawait gateway.select(sessionId, { timeoutMs: 20_000, target: css('#ferrara'), eligibility: REJECT_HIDDEN_AND_DISABLED }, 'Manage Documents');\n// fixture result line: selected Manage Documents (11)\n\nawait gateway.legacySelect(sessionId, { timeoutMs: 20_000, target: css('#ferrara'), eligibility: REJECT_DISABLED_ONLY, adjust: promoteZeroAreaPointerTarget }, 'Manage Documents');\n// fixture result line: selected Manage Documents (11)\n```\n\nThe same control under the legacy typed path and under `select`. The legacy column was measured on Grid Chrome 126 with the click, type, Enter sequence. The merged legacy path types without the click and uses the same type-ahead.\n\n| Case | Legacy typed path | `select` | Same or gap |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `Manage Documents` | `selected Manage Documents (11)` | `selected Manage Documents (11)` | same |\n| `manage documents` | `selected Manage Documents (11)` | `selected Manage Documents (11)` via the case fold | same |\n| `11` | selection unchanged, reports success | `selected Manage Documents (11)` via the value attribute | gap on purpose: value fallback |\n| `Manage Docs` | `selected Manage Documents (11)`, reports success | `SelectOptionMatchError` reason `noMatchingOption`, matchCount 0 | gap on purpose: fails closed |\n| `Create` | `selected Create Check Call (9)`, reports success | `SelectOptionMatchError` reason `noMatchingOption` | gap on purpose: no prefix match |\n| empty string | selection unchanged, reports success | `SelectOptionMatchError` reason `noMatchingOption` | gap on purpose, [BE-2969](https://linear.app/sola-ai/issue/BE-2969) |\n| `New Jersey` with two options of different values | first `New Jersey` | `SelectOptionMatchError` reason `ambiguousOption`, matchCount 2 | gap on purpose |\n| `<div role=\"listbox\">` target | click, type, Enter into the widget | `NotNativeSelectError` tagName `div` | gap on purpose: `legacySelect` covers it |\n\n## Testing\n\nGrid run of the actuation integration suite on the compose Selenium Grid (chrome-node 4.22), covering both select methods and the three legacySelect cases. The two skips are the upload and download cases that need PLAYGROUND_BASE_URL. Log noise trimmed.\n\n```text\n$ vitest run --project integration src/selenium/selenium.integration.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  27 passed | 2 skipped (29)\n   Start at  09:52:45\n   Duration  33.33s (transform 139ms, setup 0ms, import 284ms, tests 32.97s, environment 0ms)\n```\n\n- Gym engine runs pending, Cory runs them once the shared ports are free.\n",
